course: dictionary
lesson: 13211
title: Furnishing a home
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a thing or describe an action. Furnishings are things: the chairs, cushions, curtains and rugs in a room. «The shop sells soft furnishings like cushions and rugs.» The word is usually plural, furnishings, because a room has lots of them.
explain: Furnishing can also be something people do. «They are furnishing the new flat with a sofa and a table» means they are putting furniture into the room. The clue is what the people are doing to the flat. Ask yourself: is this a thing, or an action?
explain: Context tells you which meaning fits. «The furnishing of the flat took all weekend» is about the job of putting things in, because it took all weekend. A thing cannot take a weekend, but a job can.
fact: Furnishings means furniture, carpets, curtains and other things in a room or house.
fact: «Soft furnishings» means cushions, curtains and rugs.
fact: Furnishing can also mean putting furniture into a room or house.
fact: When people move house, they are furnishing the new home.
fact: In maths, a shopping problem may list furnishings with prices, so read the list carefully.
exercise: «The shop sells soft furnishings like cushions and rugs.» What are soft furnishings? | Books and pens | Cars and bicycles | Food and drinks | *Cushions, curtains and rugs
exercise: «They are furnishing the new flat with a sofa and a table.» What does furnishing mean here? | Selling the flat | *Putting furniture into the flat | Cleaning the windows | Painting the walls
exercise: «The furnishing of the flat took all weekend.» Is furnishing a thing or an action here? | A thing you can sit on | A kind of bread | *An action: putting furniture into the room | A colour of paint
test: Mum says, «We need new furnishings for the lounge.» What does she need? | Fresh bread for lunch | A new bike for school | *Curtains, rugs and other things for the room | Lessons on Saturday
test: A shop list says: rug, cushions, bicycle, curtains. Which one is NOT a furnishing? | Rug | Cushions | Curtains | *Bicycle
exam: What does furnishing mean in «Furnishing the new flat took the whole weekend»? | *Putting furniture into the room | Painting the front door | Moving the car | Cleaning the windows
